    {
      "id": "3f80a618c550ad203ff97d9a5c358856",
      "title": "Tell HN: Lots of Ask HNs again",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50649864",
      "publish_time": "2026-11-26T00:43:34",
      "views": 710,
      "comments": 71,
      "forwards": 0,
      "favorites": 161,
      "content": "There have been questions about why the &#x2F;ask page (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;ask\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;ask</a>) was running dry of Ask HNs - e.g.:<p><i>Ask HN: Why is Ask HN only showing me 14 posts?</i> - <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49984484\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49984484</a> - Oct 2026 (47 comments)<p><i>Ask HN: Why is pagination gone on &quot;Ask HN&quot;, and showing only 19 items?</i> - <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=50280719\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=50280719</a> - Oct 2026 (3 comments)<p>I believe I found the problem. The pool of stories for <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;ask\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;ask</a> has traditionally been drawn from the ranked stories list from which we generate the frontpage. That list is restricted to the top 1500 ranked submissions, and it seems the % of submissions which are text posts (i.e. no linked URL) had declined enough to starve the Ask HN feed. The solution is to compute a separate list of ranked Ask HNs.<p>p.s. &quot;Ask HN&quot; is the conventional name but it means text posts. The title can also start with &quot;Tell HN&quot; or nothing in particular. They&#x27;re just posts which were submitted without a URL.",
      "hotness": 58.0,
      "category": "趣新闻"
    },
